	(text_box "- Battery and protection: 400 mAh LiPo (BT1) feeds the VBAT rail through a 2 A slow-blow fuse (F1). C1 (220 µF) steadies the voltage during modem transmit bursts.\n- Battery sense: R1/R2 (1 MΩ each) halve VBAT for the D0 analog input, and C2 (100 nF) steadies the reading.\n- MCU: XIAO ESP32S3 (U1) is powered from VBAT through J1 to its underside BAT pads, reads the sensors, and controls the boost, modem and light.\n- Deployment detection: DRV5032 Hall switch (U4) on 3V3 tells D1 when the magnet on the cover flap moves away, meaning the MK5 has fired.\n- 5 V boost: MiniBoost (U2) turns VBAT into 5 V when D2 sets its En pin high. R3 (10 kΩ) keeps it off at startup.\n- Cellular: Stamp CatM (U3) runs on 5 V with C3 (220 µF) next to it and sends the alert over Cat-M. UART: XIAO D6 to Stamp Rx, Stamp Tx to XIAO D5.\n- Survivor light: three white LEDs (D1-D3) on 5 V, each with a 100 Ω resistor (R4-R6), switched by Q1 from D3 through R8. R7 (100 kΩ) keeps the light off at startup."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
